---
description: Evidence must show the thing under test. Always applied.
alwaysApply: true
---

When capturing evidence (`EVIDENCE=true`), the feature, row, dialog, toast, or
record under test **must be clearly visible** in the screenshot and present in
the proving moment of the video. A passing test whose media shows a blank page,
a spinner, the wrong scroll position, a closed dialog, or an unrelated screen is
**invalid evidence**. Fix the capture before publishing anything.

## While writing the spec

Playwright's default end-of-test screenshot is the final viewport, so frame the
subject deliberately:

1. Scroll it into view (`scrollIntoViewIfNeeded`, or a page-object helper).
2. Keep the proving UI open. Do not dismiss the dialog or toast that carries the
   requirement before the capture.
3. Attach a focused shot when the end state would hide it:
   `test.info().attach("screenshot", { body: await locator.screenshot(), contentType: "image/png" })`.
   The evidence reporter puts mid-test attachments first for exactly this reason.
4. End the test while the subject is still on screen, so the video contains the
   proof rather than only the setup.

## While verifying

Check the named subject of each requirement is readable in the image and present
in the video. Wrong viewport or missing subject fails that cell, even when
Playwright reported a pass.
